Description: preserve the PostgreSQL driver's original ioloop during synchronous waits
 The Debian 12 Dovecot 2.3.19.1 driver leaves orig_ioloop unset while the
 OAuth2 passdb has a live HTTP client. Starting auth then switches away from
 the OAuth client's ioloop and aborts on http_client_context_close().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dovecot/core/commit/2340275fade3af92792cd4303b8fc5945ed9d7c7
Upstream-Commit: 2340275fade3af92792cd4303b8fc5945ed9d7c7
Bug: https://dovecot.org/mailman3/hyperkitty/list/dovecot@dovecot.org/thread/WNVZVQ3OKDHRTBVZXHKIRS5MZMXR4TJC/
Last-Update: 2026-08-23
--- a/src/lib-sql/driver-pgsql.c
+++ b/src/lib-sql/driver-pgsql.c
@@ -1275 +1275 @@ static void driver_pgsql_wait(struct sql_db *_db)
-	struct ioloop *prev_ioloop = current_ioloop;
+	db->orig_ioloop = current_ioloop;
@@ -1281 +1281 @@ static void driver_pgsql_wait(struct sql_db *_db)
-	io_loop_set_current(prev_ioloop);
+	io_loop_set_current(db->orig_ioloop);
